<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#manuscript">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuscript</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A manuscript is a handwritten book or document. Manuscript traditions were central to learning and record-keeping in many empires, from the scholarly libraries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali empires</a> to illuminated works of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Surviving Aztec codices and Adal texts are also important sources for their histories.</p></div>
